Device selection in site backups
================================

A site selection and an explicit device list now both constrain the core device
query. The exported device set is their intersection within the requested
organization. Previously a nonempty device list replaced the site filter, so a
backup labeled for one site could contain device records from another site in
the same organization. A mixed list now includes only devices at the selected
site; an entirely out-of-site list produces an empty core device set.

Existing behavior is preserved for organization-wide selection, site-only
selection, duplicate IDs, foreign/missing/deleted devices and include_devices=false.
An empty list retains its existing meaning of no explicit device restriction;
this change does not redefine it to mean export no devices. No schema changes,
new privileges or dependency changes are needed.

The backup create route requires an unscoped organization administrator. This
qualification demonstrates a selection/contents defect, not cross-organization
access through that route. Missing, foreign and deleted site identifiers are
also checked directly at the collector boundary; the HTTP route has separate
site validation. Those direct cases are not an HTTP authorization claim.

Tests use actual PostgreSQL rows and the core backup contributor, with ordinary
snapshot and vault options. Separate application processes also create encrypted
local files, verify their checksum, decrypt/decompress them and inspect the device
records and manifest counts. Requested site metadata must match the archive's
selected devices. No synthetic successful result stands in for archive readback.

This correction is limited to core device selection. It does not qualify all
contributors' site scopes, credential dependency closure, device/controller/site
lifecycle consistency, concurrent authority changes, historical archives, full
fresh-install recovery, remote storage durability, vendor restoration or RTO/RPO.
Other sections of a site backup still require their own scope contract review.
Shipping/runtime evidence is separately gated and recorded.
